----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var z = 10

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var total = 0

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

set total = b + 1
set z = z + 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let shown = total * 10

----------
expect all five units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 125 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `z` = 11 |
| 3 | - | compiles, runs | new | `total` = 126 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1), updates `z` (2), overwrites `total` (3) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 5 | reads `total` (3) | compiles, runs | new | `shown` = 1260 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 1
----------

var b = 50

----------
expect unit 1 is edited
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | `b` = 50 |
| 2 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 reruns and updates `z`, which it updated when it last ran | `z` = 11 |
| 3 | - | untouched | unit 4 overwrites `total` without reading it | `total` = 51 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1), updates `z` (2), overwrites `total` (3) | reruns | reads `b` from unit 1 | - |
| 5 | reads `total` (3) | reruns | reads `total` after unit 4, which wrote a new value | `shown` = 510 |

